[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: General schematic simulation bridge

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-NETS-001
TITLE: Compile the electrical graph for the native solver
STATEMENT: >>>
The shared command shall compile the captured schematic revision into a ground-first circuit using terminal wires, equal labels and explicit junctions. Drawing coordinates shall have no effect. Ground symbols shall represent the common reference. R, L, C, independent voltage and current sources and linear E, F, G and H sources shall retain terminal order and SI values. F and H shall bind explicitly to a voltage source branch. Unsupported parts, open terminals, shorted device terminals and invalid bindings shall be refused.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
CircuitBridge, NativeCircuitSolver and BridgeTests. Native API input is bounded and never executes user commands or source text.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-RUN-001
TITLE: Execute and verify probe analyses
STATEMENT: >>>
The browser and MCP shall dispatch the same revisioned command for DC operating point, explicit AC frequency points and transient with stop and maximum step settings. AC independent-source excitation shall use explicit magnitude and phase. Transient shall support explicit bounded voltage and current pulse settings. Results shall include the original revision, probe, analysis and finite samples on the requested axis, with real and imaginary components for AC. Unavailable or incomplete results shall fail explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BrowserSmoke, McpSmoke, BridgeTests and BridgeNgspice compare the same mixed RLC lesson with an independently authored deck. General run history persistence and additional waveform forms remain separate requirements.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-MODEL-001
TITLE: Bind conduction-only diode and level 1 MOS channels
STATEMENT: >>>
The schematic bridge shall bind a diode to effective saturation current and thermal voltage. An NMOS or PMOS level 1 channel shall require an explicit instance binding and preserve drain, gate, source and bulk identity. The binding shall validate finite effective parameters, including positive beta and surface potential and nonnegative body-effect and modulation coefficients. Nonlinear transient shall select the native backward Euler profile. Unsupported model families shall produce an explicit failure.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BridgeTests verifies binding and terminal identity. BrowserSmoke, McpSmoke and BridgeNgspice exercise the diode and NMOS fixtures. Junction and channel charge, other model levels, and broader polarity and bias coverage remain open.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-DIODE-Q-001
TITLE: Bind diode depletion and diffusion charge
STATEMENT: >>>
A diode binding shall carry optional effective junction capacitance, junction potential, grading coefficient, forward coefficient and transit time. Valid nonzero storage parameters shall map to the native depletion and diffusion model for operating point, complex AC and backward Euler transient. Invalid parameter domains shall be refused before solving.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
ChargedDiodeBinding, BridgeNgspice diode-charge fixture, BrowserSmoke and McpSmoke. Avalanche, series resistance and temperature scaling are outside this profile.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-MOS1-Q-001
TITLE: Bind MOS1 body depletion and overlap charge
STATEMENT: >>>
The bridge shall map effective MOS1 gate overlap capacitances and body depletion parameters to explicit native companions. The body junction polarity shall follow the transistor polarity. An equipotential companion shall contribute no element. Invalid storage parameter domains shall be refused. Intrinsic channel charge is outside this profile.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Mos1OverlapAndBodyCharge, BridgeNgspice mos1-charge fixture, BrowserSmoke and McpSmoke.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-BJT-001
TITLE: Bind a three-terminal bipolar conduction model
STATEMENT: >>>
The bridge shall preserve collector, base and emitter identity and require explicit saturation current, forward and reverse gain, and effective thermal voltages. It shall lower the three-terminal conduction profile into native junctions and signed controlled branches, with private nodes counted against the circuit limit. Invalid parameters or missing models shall fail before solving.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BjtRequiresExplicitModel, BridgeNgspice bjt fixture, BrowserSmoke and McpSmoke. Charge storage, substrate, series resistances, and full Gummel-Poon behavior remain outside this profile.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-BSIM330-001
TITLE: Bind bulk BSIM3 3.3.0 through a trusted native provider
STATEMENT: >>>
The bridge shall validate explicit bulk BSIM3 geometry and effective model parameters, preserve drain, gate, source and bulk order, and reject a simultaneous MOS1 binding. Analysis shall use the host-configured native provider for DC, AC and transient. A sheet or command shall have no mechanism to select executable module paths.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BulkBsim330Requires, BridgeNgspice bsim3 fixture, BrowserSmoke and McpSmoke. This profile excludes SOI, arbitrary model cards and unqualified bias ranges.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-BJT-Q-001
TITLE: Bind base junction depletion and transit storage
STATEMENT: >>>
A bipolar binding shall accept independent base-emitter and base-collector junction storage. Each storage contribution shall preserve polarity and remain outside the conduction sense branch so the transport gain does not amplify displacement current. The bridge shall validate the physical domain before execution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verified on a resistor-loaded NPN with a finite base drive resistance. The profile retains bounded Ebers-Moll conduction.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-WAVEFORMS-001
TITLE: Execute inline PWL, damped sine and exponential sources
STATEMENT: >>>
The bridge shall support inline ordered PWL, damped sine and exponential overrides for independent sources with SI times and values, phase in degrees and bounded payloads. It shall refuse duplicate source assignments across waveform families and refuse nonfinite and invalid parameters. Browser and MCP shall use the same typed analysis request.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BridgeTests, BrowserSmoke, McpSmoke and BridgeNgspice. File assets and stochastic sources are outside this requirement.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-SOI-FD-001
TITLE: Execute the pinned four-terminal FD-SOI profile
STATEMENT: >>>
The bridge shall bind an explicitly selected NMOS SOI instance to the pinned four-terminal native model and preserve drain, gate, source and back gate identity. The schematic body contact shall be left unconnected. The binding shall admit DC operating point and refuse AC or transient before invoking the native solver.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
SoiBridgeTests, BrowserSmoke, McpSmoke and BridgeNgspice fd-soi. Arbitrary SOI cards, PMOS, body-contact models and charge-dependent analyses remain separate.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-SETTINGS-001
TITLE: Persist and transfer analysis entry settings
STATEMENT: >>>
A saved sheet shall retain bounded model, waveform and analysis entry fields. Reload and undo shall restore the applicable fields, and older sheets shall use defaults. MCP shall read fields and apply a bounded batch atomically. Importing entry fields shall not bypass model validation at execution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BridgeSettingsTests, BrowserSmoke and McpSmoke. These are sheet-local settings rather than a named reusable model definition store.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-DC-STEP-001
TITLE: Select bounded DC source continuation
STATEMENT: >>>
An explicit DC source-continuation request shall use the bounded native source-stepping policy. It shall preserve the full-source operating point and refuse the policy on other analysis modes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BridgeNgspice mos1-high and browser and MCP high-bias runs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BRIDGE-MODEL-LIB-001
TITLE: Save and reuse named model definitions
STATEMENT: >>>
A sheet shall store a bounded collection of case-insensitive named model definitions separately from instance settings. Typed commands shall list, define, remove and apply definitions through the browser and MCP. Applying a definition shall copy its parameters to a compatible instance without changing other instance bindings. Loading an older sheet without definitions shall yield an empty library. Invalid definitions shall not change the current sheet.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
BridgeSettingsTests, BrowserSmoke and McpSmoke. The supported families are diode, BJT, MOS1 and BSIM3. Applying a definition creates an instance-local copy; later edits to the definition do not change existing bindings. MCP can transfer definitions between sheets by reading and defining them.
<<<
